Part 1 FEC default fix

changed: harness/src/sender.cpp Config::fec_k default is now 0.
meaning: default sender sends raw frames with no FEC envelope and no parity datagrams.

byte-identical verification:
source: commit 5dc3d3c sender copied shm frame bytes into batch.frames and sent batch.frames[i].data() with batch.lengths[i].
source: current sender with cfg.fec_k == 0 increments fec_data_bytes by len and calls emit_datagram(frame, len), which calls direct_send(data, len). No fec::data_datagram call is made and no envelope is prefixed.
runtime: raw default smoke without --fec-k passed. Sender startup printed fec_k=0. Sender exit printed fec_parity_sent=0, fec_data_bytes=319872, fec_parity_bytes=0, fec_overhead_pct=0.000000. Receiver printed received=1000, published=1000, fec_parity_received=0, fec_recovered=0.
limitation: this verifies datagram payload path by source and raw receiver behavior. It does not pcap-compare old and new binaries byte by byte because the pre-FEC binary was not preserved.

