unit test:
command: make -C harness && make -C harness test
result: PASS
unit output included test_fec_disabled_raw_stream OK and ALL TESTS PASSED

new test: test_fec_disabled_raw_stream feeds raw frames to fec::Decoder and asserts parity_received=0 and recovered=0.

other default or default-behavior changes versus commit 5dc3d3c:
1. receiver now enables sliding-window dedupe by default. Old receiver used last_seq gating. This changes behavior for reordered packets, but it fixes a correctness bug. I do not recommend reverting it; keep --dedupe-disable for A/B.
2. sender no longer exposes or uses the old default batching path: --batch-size default 32 and --batch-timeout-us default 50 existed in 5dc3d3c. Current sender sends datagrams one at a time through direct_send. This can change syscall rate and timing even when FEC is off. I recommend restoring raw batching or preserving equivalent batching for --fec-k 0 if exact baseline behavior matters.
3. new sender instrumentation defaults are inert: --test-drop-pct=0, --test-reorder-pct=0, --test-reorder-delay-us=0, --test-seed=1. No revert recommended.
4. receiver has new --fec-gens default 64. It only affects FEC envelopes; raw frames pass through because fec::Decoder publishes unknown magic/raw datagrams. No revert recommended.
